\begin{proof}
For each positive piece, Theorem~\ref{f9tf:measure} gives
\[
 |\nu_{w_{a,\epsilon},Q_i\eta}|
 \leq c_i p_{t_f(V),0}(\eta)\nu_{w_{a,\epsilon},\theta_i}.
\]
The mass of the positive measure on the right is $T_{w_{a,\epsilon}}(\theta_i)$. Equation~\eqref{eq:firstlimit} bounds it by
$T_{w_a}(\theta_i)+\epsilon\log m_a\,|\mu_{U,\DD\theta_i}|(U)$.
Summing with $|q_a|$ proves \eqref{eq:uniformmass}. The limit measures satisfy the analogous bound. For a fixed $\beta$, decompose it into finitely many stage images; subadditivity of total variation gives $M_{u,\beta}$. Their supports are contained in $\supp\beta$ by Theorem~\ref{f9tf:measure}, independently of $\epsilon$.

For every ordinary smooth $h$, the exact scalar identity and \eqref{eq:error} give
\begin{equation}\label{eq:smoothrate}
 \left|\int h\,d(\nu_{u_\epsilon,\beta}-\nu_{u,\beta})\right|
 =|T_{u_\epsilon-u}(h\beta)|
 \leq\epsilon D_u\,|\mu_{U,\DD(h\beta)}|(U).
\end{equation}
For a continuous $v$ on $\supp\beta$, choose ordinary smooth $h$ approximating it uniformly there, using the finite-partition density in Theorem~\ref{f9tf:measure}. The difference of the pairings with $v$ is bounded by
\begin{equation}\label{eq:continuousrate}
 2M_{u,\beta}\|v-h\|_{\supp\beta}
       +\epsilon D_u\,|\mu_{U,\DD(h\beta)}|(U).
\end{equation}
First choose $h$, then let $\epsilon\downarrow0$. This proves convergence on every continuous test, with no radial restriction. Finally, the extra difference caused by $v_\epsilon-v$ is at most
$M_{u,\beta}\|v_\epsilon-v\|_{\supp\beta}$, proving \eqref{eq:joint}. All support, mass and stage bounds required for this passage have been exhibited.
\end{proof}

